### lin-spring-shiro-jwt — Apache Shiro 2 + JWT (slim token) REST API
### Base URL
@host = http://localhost:8080

### =====================================================
### 1. Login as admin (seed: admin/admin123)
# expect 200 + accessToken (slim: sub/iat/exp only)
# store token: adminLogin
# @name adminLogin
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### 2. Login as user (seed: user/user123)
# @name userLogin
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "user",
  "password": "user123"
}

### =====================================================
### Slim token + Redis authority cache
### Prerequisite: Redis running on localhost:6379
###   docker run -d --name redis -p 6379:6379 redis:7
### Inspect cache with: redis-cli GET auth:authorities:admin
### =====================================================

### 3. Current user info (authorities resolved via JwtRealm -> AuthorityResolver)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. Token stays slim - decode the middle segment, only sub/iat/exp inside
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5. List users — @RequiresPermissions("user:read"), both roles have it
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6. Admin stats — @RequiresRoles("ADMIN"), user gets 403 JSON
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. Admin stats with admin token -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8. Audit — @RequiresPermissions("admin:read"): user 403, admin 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9. Delete user — @RequiresPermissions("user:write"): user 403, admin 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/users/2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 10. Evict authority cache for 'user' (permission changes take effect on next request)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/admin/authority-cache/user
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### =====================================================
### Failure paths — uniform ApiError JSON
### =====================================================

### 11. No token -> 401 (written by JwtFilter)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me

### 12. Tampered token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}x

### 13. Wrong password -> 401 (AuthenticationException -> GlobalExceptionHandler)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 14. Validation error -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "",
  "password": "x"
}

### 15. Permission revocation demo:
###  a) open H2 console, run: DELETE FROM user_roles WHERE user_id = (SELECT id FROM users WHERE username='user')
###  b) GET /users with the user token -> still 200 (cached authorities)
###  c) run request 10 above to evict
###  d) run this request again -> 403 (authorities reloaded from DB, now empty)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
